# WCAG 2.2 Level AA

- **Semantics:** Use native `<button>`, `<a>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<dialog>`. Never put click handlers on `<div>` / `<span>`.
- **Headings:** One `<h1>` per page; keep heading levels sequential.
- **Contrast:** Normal text ≥ **4.5:1**; large text (18pt+ / 14pt+ bold) and UI boundaries/icons ≥ **3:1**.
- **Focus visible:** Do not use `outline-none` without a high-contrast `focus-visible:ring-*` (or equivalent) replacement.
- **Focus not obscured (2.4.11):** Sticky headers/banners must not fully cover focused targets; use `scroll-margin-top` (or similar) as needed.
- **Target size (2.5.8):** Interactive targets ≥ **24×24 CSS px** or adequate spacing from adjacent targets.
- **Labels:** Every input/select/textarea needs a linked `<label for>` or `aria-label`. Icon-only buttons need an accessible name. Use `aria-live="polite"` for status/errors.
- **Tab order:** Do not use `tabindex` greater than `0`.
